course: dictionary
lesson: 7022
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: Some words can be a thing and an action. Parrot can be a noun, a bird, or a verb, to repeat someone's words without understanding them. The sentence around the word tells you which job it has. «Parrots are among the cleverest birds.» Here a parrot is a bird, a thing.
explain: Now look at the verb: «Ben parroted his teacher's answer without knowing what it meant.» Ben did something, and he did not understand what he said. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Ben repeated his teacher's answer without understanding it" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Ask two questions. Is it a thing or an action? Does the meaning fit the whole sentence? «Think of a parrot climbing its cage: beak, foot, beak, foot.» This parrot is a bird doing an action, and the word beak tells you it is a bird's body.
fact: A parrot is a bird with bright colours and a curved beak.
fact: Some parrots can copy words and sounds.
fact: «Macaws» are the biggest parrots, and the hyacinth macaw is about a metre long from beak to tail.
fact: «A parrot's hooked beak and strong jaw crack hard nuts and seeds.»
fact: To parrot is to repeat someone's words without understanding them, and talk like a parrot means the same thing.
exercise: «Parrots are among the cleverest birds.» In this sentence, what is a parrot? | *A kind of bird | A kind of fish | A type of tree | A bright colour
exercise: «Ben parroted his teacher's answer without knowing what it meant.» What does parroted mean? | Asked a brand new question | *Repeated words without understanding them | Shouted the answer loudly | Wrote the answer very neatly
exercise: «A parrot's hooked beak and strong jaw crack hard nuts and seeds.» Find and copy the word for the parrot's hard mouth part. | nuts | *beak | seeds | cracks
test: «The pirate's parrot talked to everyone on the ship.» In this sentence, what is a parrot? | *A bird | A kind of ship | A pirate's hat | To repeat without understanding
test: «Real sailors brought parrots home from tropical voyages.» What did the sailors do with parrots? | Hid them in their cabins | *Brought them home from tropical voyages | Fed them only fish | Painted them bright colours
exam: Which sentence uses parrot as a verb? | *«Mia parroted every word the teacher said without thinking.» | «Parrots live in warm forests and eat fruit.» | «The parrot sat on its perch and whistled.» | «The parrot had bright blue and green feathers.»
